    "title": "Jiří Procházka vs. Carlos Ulberg: How to watch UFC 327 tonight, full fight card and more",
    "text": "Jiri Prochazka will fight Carlos Ulberg at UFC 327 this Saturday, here's how to watch. (Stephen R. Sylvanie-Imagn Images) (IMAGN IMAGES via Reuters Connect / Reuters)Former champion Jiří Procházka is currently the light heavyweight division’s No. 2-ranked contender, and he's pitted against No. 3 Carlos Ulberg at UFC 327 this weekend in a title fight for the light heavyweight UFC belt vacated by Alex Pereira. Pereira announced in March his intention to now compete as a heavyweight. UFC 327 will be held at Miami’s Kaseya Center on Saturday, April 11, with early prelims starting at 5:30 p.m. ET, prelims at 7 p.m. ET and the main card at 9 p.m. ET.Jiří Procházka vs. Carlos Ulberg and every other match on the fight card will stream on Paramount+, while some of the night's fights will also be broadcast on CBS from 8 - 10 p.m. ET. The fights will also be available on Paramount+ on demand after it concludes. Here’s everything you need to know about how to watch UFC 327, including the full fight card, schedule and more.AdvertisementHow to watch the Jiri Prochazka vs. Carlos Ulberg fightDate: Saturday, April 11Start time: Event begins at 5 p.m. ETFight time (approximate): Main card fights begin at 9 p.m. ETLocation: Kaseya Center, MiamiTV channel: CBSStreaming: Paramount+The UFC 327 fight between Jiří Procházka and Carlos Ulberg is this Saturday, April 11 at 9 p.m. ET.What channel is the Jiří Procházka vs. Carlos Ulberg fight on?Select portions of the UFC 327 fight card will be broadcast on CBS from 8 - 10 p.m. ET. You can tune in to CBS on platforms like DirecTV and Hulu + Live TV.AdvertisementWhere to watch the Jiří Procházka vs. Carlos Ulberg fightThe complete UFC 327 fight card headlined by Jiří Procházka and Carlos Ulberg is available with a subscription to Paramount+.Paramount+ offers subscribers access to loads of sports from Champions League soccer to the NFL, and now it's your one-stop shop for all things UFC, with no added Pay-Per-View fees. You can catch the upcoming UFC 327 event and every other fight card on the schedule for the price of a Paramount+ subscription. Paramount+ subscriptions are available in monthly and annual options. Additionally, there are two subscription plans to choose from: Paramount+ Essential ($8.99/month) and Paramount+ Premium ($13.99/month). UFC 327 Fight CardMain card#2 Jiří Procházka (32-5-1) vs. #3 Carlos Ulberg (14-1-0) - light heavyweight title bout#4 Curtis Blaydes (19-5-0) vs. Josh Hokit (8-0-0) – heavyweight bout#10 Dominick Reyes (15-5-0) vs. #12 Johnny Walker (22-9-0) – light heavyweight bout#6 Azamat Murzakanov (16-0-0) vs. #14 Paulo Costa (15-4-0) – light heavyweight boutUFC Hall of Famer Cub Swanson (31-14-0) vs. Nate Landwehr (18-7-0) – featherweight boutPrelims#13 Patricio Pitbull (37-8-0) vs. Aaron Pico (13-5-0) – featherweight bout#8 Mateusz Gamrot (25-4-0) vs. Esteban Ribovics (15-2-0) – lightweight boutKevin Holland (28-15-0) vs. Randy Brown (20-7-0) – welterweight bout#2 Tatiana Suarez (12-109) vs. #6 Loopy Godinez (14-5-0) – women’s strawweight boutEarly prelimsChris Padilla (17-6-0) vs. MarQuel Mederos (11-1-0) — lightweight boutUFC Hall of Famer Kelvin Gastelum (21-10-0) vs. Vicente Luque (23-12-1) – middleweight boutCharles Radtke (11-5-0) vs. Francisco Prado (12-4-0) — welterweight bout",
